[{:seon.task/name "design-writes-the-implement-steps-proofs"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `my.task/update!` edits only this agent's own :seon.task/plan or :seon.task/instructions, and `seon.merge/carried-platform-attrs` carries only those two, so the proofs a design step writes for implement reach main only as plan text. Reproduction: a staged request with no proofs (`seon.template/stages`); design writes red deftests and rewrites its plan; implement is refused :no-proofs by `seon.reconcile/done-explain` (docs/tasks.md). Cause: no function edits another task's members, and proofs are not carried. Correct (DESIGN-tasks §5.2, prototyped): ``my.task/edit!`` (id f & args: clojure.core/update on any authored member of any task, written on the branch), and :seon.task/proofs among what `seon.task/carry-tx` carries. Deletes: `my.task/update!`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-test/edit-writes-another-tasks-proofs seon.reconcile-test/implement-holds-the-proofs-design-wrote}}
{:seon.task/name "a-task-merges-from-its-data"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-11-08: \"I want to be able to go from a fresh chat session to work being done and merged\", and kinds go (\"look for explicit data or metadata\"). Built on jolt/task-merges and proved in parts (not landed): seon.task/merges? from the task's data, a task merging itself unless a task that needs it works the same branch (a staged template's merge task), replacing the kind set #{:merge :whole}; seon.reconcile's :merging mark for any task judged ready or at its gate; :merged among the outcomes a message wakes, so a message reopens a merged task (its first turn merges main from the commit main merged, f25b21f2f4); seon.reconcile/done-explain's :no-proofs only for a branch that changed something (:changed, the count of program keys changed since its base, from the writer's read and the status's changes). Proofs written: seon.reconcile-test/a-task-merges-when-its-proofs-are-green-whatever-template-made-it, seon.reconcile-test/a-message-reopens-a-merged-task. Withdrawn from landing: it breaks seon.agent-test/a-woken-agent-that-replies-stays-parked (bisected to it, green on main): a woken :user task that only replies is judged :done, :lost or :merged instead of :parked, even with :open restored. Not yet found: the turn loop's merge? is now true for a chat (seon.turn: merge main at a green end, merge-turns, seon.reconcile/hairy); a fix counting merge turns only for a :merge task or unmerged entries did not cure it. Next: rebase onto Context's namespace split (status now in seon/ctx/status.clj), read what the chat's end outcome and its judgment's inputs actually are with that test, fix at the cause; then remove :open by data (a task with no proofs whose branch changed nothing parks). The jolt/land-1108b branch holds the latest state with the test fixes."
